<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Mithridatic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">89–85 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Mithridatic War was fought from 89 to 85 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a>. Mithridates overran Roman Asia, ordered the massacre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and Italians there in 88 BCE and won over many Greek cities, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> took Athens and defeated his armies at Chaeronea and Orchomenus, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-dardanos">Treaty of Dardanos</a> restored the pre-war frontiers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-mithridatic-war.jpg" alt="First Mithridatic War" width="320" height="141" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ifly6 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_asia,_eve_of_First_Mithridatic_war.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
